1
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,390
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:09,790
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,070
♪Set reality aside♪

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,390
♪Follow your heart♪

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,750
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,230
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,110
♪Just be a little braver♪

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,870
♪Come closer, come closer♪

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:23,950
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

10
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,070
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,790
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,820
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,780
(A music restaurant in Beijing)

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,520
Did everyone see what's in the box?

15
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,360
Check yours.

16
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:42,440
I did. Are these from you?

17
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,480
I was just about to say that.

18
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,280
I didn't really know what everyone

19
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,720
is like,

20
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:50,320
or what everyone's style is,

21
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:51,680
so I picked out something

22
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,120
(Cat-shaped tableware for everyone)
that everyone can use,

23
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,280
no matter their personality.

24
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:55,520
I love it.

25
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:57,480
I'll think of you every time I eat.

26
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:00,880
So cute.

27
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:01,920
We have the same one.

28
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,160
Yeah, that's because

29
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:04,160
they come in six pairs.

30
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:05,080
That's right.

31
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:06,280
It's kind of like a blind box.

32
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:07,560
You don't know which one you'll get.

33
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,160
Thank you so much.

34
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,960
One of the boxes should have

35
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:17,460
two extra.

36
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,060
(One special gift box)
Little sauce dishes.

37
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:19,920
There's a surprise box.

38
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,280
Looks like we didn't get it.

39
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,160
Let's see which of the guys got it.

40
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,000
The lucky one.

41
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:29,680
The lucky one? Which lucky one?

42
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,280
Exactly.

43
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,800
(Noticing)
Don't be nervous.

44
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,200
We're all staring at her.

45
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,640
It's okay.
We've all been staring at you.

46
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,240
Yeah, all of us are staring at you.

47
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,320
It's fine.

48
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:45,440
I'm staring at you pretty girls too.

49
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,040
No problem.

50
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,120
But I'm curious

51
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,720
what everyone does around the house.

52
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,320
Cooking.

53
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:54,520
That's great.

54
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:55,320
You can cook?

55
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,840
I can cook a little.

56
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,960
She made fish yesterday.

57
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,040
And it was really good.

58
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,120
Not fishy at all.

59
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,360
Thank you.

60
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:08,160
Two of the guys told us yesterday

61
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,640
that each of our rooms could

62
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:10,880
make one dish.

63
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:11,520
That's right.

64
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:11,880
They didn't know.

65
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,720
Who said that?

66
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,680
That could actually work.

67
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,840
One dish per room could work.

68
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,120
Yeah, one dish from each room.

69
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:18,680
That could really work.

70
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,120
Let's try it.

71
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,200
Make it a competition.

72
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,960
Chen Hewen and Cui Yihang.

73
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,720
That's right.

74
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,360
The two of them suggested

75
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,880
that each room make one dish

76
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,480
and have a cook-off.

77
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:29,720
(The only one in)
Yesterday I was thinking

78
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,640
(the girls' three-person room)
the pressure was all on me.

79
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,440
But luckily you showed up.

80
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:34,200
(Heaven-sent savior)

81
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,120
We've got Sha Yue'er.

82
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,440
I told them we've got
Sha Yue'er in our room.

83
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:36,920
(Got this in the bag)
Stop it.

84
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,760
I've already won.

85
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,680
So does everyone have

86
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,120
any food preferences?

87
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,680
Like, do you eat spicy food or not?

88
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,880
Or do you like sweet things?

89
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:47,960
Honestly, it's a mix.

90
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,600
It probably depends on the dish.

91
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:51,960
With more than a dozen of us eating,

92
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,760
we'd need a really big table.

93
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:54,480
So we said when we get back,

94
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,960
we'd push the tables together.

95
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:59,040
We were just about to try it.

96
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:01,040
Can we eat at the dining table?

97
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,240
That's the living room.

98
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,320
The living room.

99
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,760
Move everything over there

100
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,440
and sit on the floor?

101
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,240
They're here.

102
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,040
Hello, everyone.

103
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,160
Hello, everyone.

104
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:26,080
Hi.

105
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,200
Hi, everyone.

106
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,320
Hi, everyone.

107
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:32,960
Hi, everyone.

108
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,480
Hi, everyone.

109
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:37,760
I'll sit over here.

110
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,200
Sure.

111
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:38,640
Okay.

112
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,260
(Everyone sits down)

113
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:43,960
This one.

114
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:45,760
(Picks it up)

115
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:49,040
Is this a gift from our new friend?

116
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:50,760
Yeah.

117
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:52,800
I'm the new one who joined today,

118
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,940
the one who came in late.

119
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,560
Let's see what you got.

120
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,440
I'm just curious.

121
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:58,800
Go ahead and open it.

122
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,800
Let me take a look.

123
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:00,760
Okay.

124
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,000
They said one is different, right?

125
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,160
There's a hidden one.

126
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:08,480
That's right.

127
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:10,040
One person's will be different.

128
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:23,740
(Leans in for a look)

129
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:28,460
(Looking)

130
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:29,560
What kind of little bowl is that?

131
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:34,920
His is...

132
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:36,460
(Turns to look)

133
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:38,940
(Cao Yiheng got the special gift box)
His is a full set.

134
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:47,720
I think tableware has a nice meaning.

135
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,880
It means joining the group

136
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:53,000
and eating together every day.

137
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,720
I think that's romantic in its own way.

138
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,520
Welcome, welcome.

139
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:00,160
So thoughtful. Welcome.

140
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:03,800
Welcome.

141
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,720
When you got here,

142
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,400
did you pick one of the color cards?

143
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,280
I did.

144
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,000
I picked blue (Empathetic Love).

145
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:11,360
Yeah.

146
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,320
I picked blue (Empathetic Love).

147
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,000
We're blue (Empathetic Love).

148
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,940
- Blue (Empathetic Love), raise your hand.
- Blue Space (Empathetic Love).

149
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,120
Blue (Empathetic Love).

150
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,440
Same wavelength.

151
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:23,000
I still can't shake
the "independent" curse.

152
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,800
Just stay independent, then.

153
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,880
I switched to dailies today.

154
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,280
Aren't dailies more comfortable?

155
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,120
So much more comfortable.

156
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,080
See? I told you.

157
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,800
My six-month contacts were torture.

158
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,400
I told you.

159
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,160
I told you yesterday

160
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,240
you should wear dailies.

161
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,120
What do you want to eat?

162
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:45,460
(Looking)

163
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:47,320
See anything you want over there?

164
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,360
I can grab it for you.

165
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,360
It's fine. I can eat anything here.

166
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,360
I'm not that hungry yet.

167
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:56,280
So with your medical studies,

168
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:58,120
you're graduating this year
and planning on grad school?

169
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:01,240
Are you planning on getting a PhD?

170
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:01,960
Maybe.

171
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,480
What area are you studying?

172
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,160
For grad school,
I'm studying basic medicine.

173
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,840
I switched from pathology to physiology.

174
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,400
Lab work and things like that.

175
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:13,360
Actually, I think we're pretty similar.

176
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,800
When I was studying sculpture,

177
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:17,520
I actually studied human muscles

178
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,520
and bones.

179
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,600
So when did you start

180
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,640
studying art?

181
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,640
Senior year.

182
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,960
You only started then?

183
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,320
It's more exam-oriented then.

184
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:30,200
But back in middle school,

185
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,320
I'd draw little things here and there.

186
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,120
I see.

187
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,520
Any plans tomorrow?

188
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,360
I have to go back to school next Friday.

189
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,280
Back to school next Friday?

190
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:40,520
We have graduation exams.

191
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,960
The exam is at eight.

192
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,440
I have to get up a little after six.

193
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,720
Your exam's around eight?

194
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:48,800
For dinner tomorrow,

195
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:49,760
is there anything you want to eat?

196
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:50,540
(Asking on his own)

197
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,640
Anything's fine.

198
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,240
Anything?

199
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,160
I'll eat anything.

200
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,960
I think I could take

201
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:58,280
a bit more time and learn how to make

202
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,080
Eight Treasure tofu.

203
00:06:59,080 --> 00:06:59,680
Okay.

204
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,520
And let everyone try it.

205
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:02,400
Sure.

206
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,960
Let's show them our Tianjin specialty.

207
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:04,360
Sounds good.

208
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,880
You'll do most of it?

209
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:06,480
Yeah.

210
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,000
I'll just...

211
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:07,640
I'll go learn it.

212
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,840
I'll help out.

213
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,240
Just tell me what to do.

214
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:12,420
(Smiles)

215
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,400
Did you notice I changed my bangs?

216
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,800
Wasn't your hair pushed back yesterday?

217
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:18,760
But the bangs are different.

218
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:19,600
Today it's a side part.

219
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,520
Yesterday was a middle part.

220
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:22,740
(Staring)

221
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,160
You didn't notice. Fine.

222
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:30,880
I can tell.

223
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:32,760
Because I've been sitting beside you.

224
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:33,680
Okay then.

225
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,680
I've got it memorized now.

226
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,960
So tomorrow,

227
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,560
you can ask me again.

228
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:49,560
Can anyone sing a Jay Chou song?

229
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,920
Want to sing one together?

230
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,540
(Extends an invitation)

231
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:56,560
"Sweetness."

232
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,840
Is that okay? Do you know it?

233
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,000
How about "Common Jasmine Orange"?

234
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,480
I don't really know that one either.

235
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,920
"Counterclockwise?"

236
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,240
(Asking)
Anything you want to sing?

237
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:10,840
I...

238
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:11,880
Everyone's way too good.

239
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,120
It's fine.

240
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,480
We're all just messing around.

241
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,320
I think your voice sounds

242
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:16,840
kind of like Eric Chou's.

243
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,400
Really?

244
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,880
Yeah, it's impressive.

245
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,000
Thank you.

246
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:23,880
You're too kind.

247
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,240
Really.

248
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,760
You're too kind.

249
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:30,520
Look at Meng.

250
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:36,800
♪I asked why♪

251
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:40,440
♪That girl sent me a message♪

252
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,240
"What I Miss."

253
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:50,800
♪But why did I smile bitterly
and say I understood♪

254
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:54,600
♪Pride so often drags us down♪

255
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:57,680
♪And sends love down winding roads♪

256
00:08:57,680 --> 00:09:03,320
♪We pretend to understand
because the truth is too bare♪

257
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,720
♪Feeling pathetic hurts
more than losing♪

258
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:09,480
♪What I miss is
talking about everything♪

259
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:12,840
♪What I miss is dreaming together♪

260
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:16,000
♪What I miss is that even after a fight♪

261
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,960
♪I still had the urge to love you♪

262
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:23,320
♪I remember that birthday♪

263
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:26,560
♪And I remember that song♪

264
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:28,360
♪I remember that starry sky♪

265
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,080
♪The tightest grip of your right hand♪

266
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,600
♪The warmest chest to lean on♪

267
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,760
♪I let go♪

268
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,320
That was amazing.

269
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:37,880
So good.

270
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,120
That sounded great.

271
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,880
You're all mic hogs here.

272
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,040
I was so nervous.

273
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:46,160
I've noticed you're all so modest.

274
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,040
Do you want to sing?

275
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,160
Is singing one of your hobbies?

276
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,440
That's not really my thing.

277
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,720
Crosstalk is, though.

278
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,840
(Teasing)
Then you'll have to show us later.

279
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,880
That's hard to do on the spot.

280
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,560
I'll be your straight man.

281
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,080
I'll sing one.

282
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:07,880
Go ahead.

283
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,620
(Stands up)

284
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,760
Do you think he's singing to you?

285
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:11,920
No.

286
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:16,960
