00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,360
But honestly, I think

582
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:53,360
it's pretty obvious
how he feels about you.

583
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:55,900
(Covers her mouth and smiles)

584
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:00,600
How was today?

585
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,480
Today was good.

586
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,760
Happiness level maxed out.

587
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,600
I think you're really happy.

588
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:07,600
You can tell that too?

589
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:07,840
Yeah.

590
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,560
Your happiness is like a shooting star

591
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,640
that suddenly hit you.

592
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:14,440
That description is
actually pretty fitting.

593
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:15,880
This is a

594
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,120
happy little room.

595
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:17,840
Right.

596
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:20,920
You've got this.

597
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,320
I'm already shipping you two.

598
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,360
Already shipping us?

599
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,000
Yeah, I'm already shipping you two.

600
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:26,440
Almost there.

601
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,920
Shipping us already?

602
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:30,520
There are already signs.

603
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:31,440
Don't hesitate.

604
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,000
Yeah, don't hesitate.

605
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,960
Why hesitate about something like this?

606
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,640
You can't hesitate.

607
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,680
Hesitate and it's over.

608
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,840
I did some serious thinking.

609
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,680
And?

610
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,320
Today you...

611
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,760
I was a little more forward.

612
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,280
My art project for today.

613
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:57,000
From an artistic perspective,
do you have

614
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:57,600
any thoughts?

615
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,640
I think it could use a bit more.

616
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,320
Color?

617
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,520
But there's no color left.

618
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:02,160
I mean more of it.

619
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:02,800
Make it denser.

620
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:03,240
Exactly.

621
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:05,080
But this way,

622
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:06,680
there's a certain beauty

623
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:07,840
in the negative space.

624
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:10,480
I get it.

625
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:11,960
Fill it all in.

626
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,080
It's more like

627
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,080
a border around it now.

628
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:17,920
It would actually look great hung up.

629
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:22,640
So now you just need to fill it in more.

630
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,260
(Zhao Xilun and Sha Yue'er,
The Courageous date)

631
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:32,520
Slime.

632
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:39,160
Did you ever make things
with dough at school?

633
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,840
Yeah, I've made things
like that at home.

634
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:42,920
Don't you think rolling out dough

635
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,680
is really therapeutic?

636
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:45,760
I'm not good at it.

637
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:46,760
I'm not good at it either.

638
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:49,760
It's really starting to set.

639
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:51,760
Yeah, we have to keep stirring.

640
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:52,360
There's no rush.

641
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:52,800
Okay.

642
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:53,640
Keep stirring until

643
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,000
it stops sticking to the sides.

644
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,760
It'll come together.

645
00:21:56,760 --> 00:21:57,200
Yeah.

646
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:57,880
Want me to take over?

647
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,640
Okay.

648
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,360
You're tired. Take a break.

649
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:00,360
I'm fine.

650
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,960
But it gets harder to stir later on.

651
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,600
I can stir it for you.

652
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:04,620
(Laughs)

653
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:07,760
Did you guys chat when you got back?

654
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:08,720
Not much.

655
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:09,200
Just went to sleep?

656
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:10,640
But we did talk for a bit.

657
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,800
Really? About what?

658
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:12,680
Just everything.

659
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:14,240
Our personal lives,

660
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:16,520
and what life's been like
since we got here.

661
00:22:16,520 --> 00:22:17,200
All of it.

662
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:19,320
Nice. We do that too.

663
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:23,960
What's your blood type?

664
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,360
How many times have I asked you this?

665
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:26,080
Third time.

666
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:26,840
What's yours?

667
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:27,520
I remember you asking three times.

668
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,120
You didn't answer me yesterday.

669
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:29,160
Yeah.

670
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:31,240
Think back to that conversation.

671
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,160
You said mosquitoes love you, right?

672
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:34,840
Mosquitoes love me.

673
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:36,240
And I remember you said

674
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,080
you're type O.

675
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:37,600
You're type B.

676
00:22:37,600 --> 00:22:38,600
Right, I'm type B.

677
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:39,920
And I said they

678
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:40,720
wouldn't bite you guys.

679
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:41,320
They'd all come for me.

680
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:42,080
Look.

681
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:44,440
Same here. Look.

682
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:45,920
So you attract them too.

683
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,280
I'm type O.

684
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:48,080
Type O?

685
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:49,560
I get bitten really easily.

686
00:22:49,560 --> 00:22:50,480
Yeah.

687
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,640
Compared to when you were a kid,

688
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,520
personality-wise,

689
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:57,160
do you think you've changed a lot?

690
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,280
I think so.

691
00:22:58,280 --> 00:22:59,760
What were you like as a kid?

692
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:01,960
Pretty wild.

693
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:03,280
Like what you described yesterday?

694
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:03,720
Yeah.

695
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:04,920
Climbing all over the place.

696
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:08,400
Like Spider-Man, the city hero.

697
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,120
Spider-Man?

698
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:09,960
Spider-Woman.

699
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,880
I really like Spider-Man.

700
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,160
I used to imagine myself

701
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:17,240
shooting webs between buildings.

702
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:21,120
It was really relaxing.

703
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:23,360
But the main reason

704
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,640
I like Spider-Man is that he

705
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:25,760
feels down-to-earth.

706
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:27,000
Down-to-earth?

707
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,480
Yeah.

708
00:23:28,060 --> 00:23:29,340
(Nods)

709
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,600
So with your parents,

710
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:33,480
how do you usually communicate?

711
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,320
Pretty well. More like friends.

712
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:36,600
You talk as equals?

713
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:37,000
Yeah.

714
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:39,840
So are you the type

715
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:41,320
who keeps things bottled up,

716
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,840
or do you have a way to let it out?

717
00:23:43,840 --> 00:23:45,230
Crying.

718
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,280
That's actually pretty healthy.

719
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:47,800
It works really well.

720
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:48,480
Crying really does help.

721
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:49,680
Crying and sleeping.

722
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:51,120
Just don't go to sleep
right after crying.

723
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:52,080
I'll feel worse if I sleep
right after crying.

724
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:53,560
You'll get a headache, right?

725
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:54,400
Yeah.

726
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:56,840
Should we take a look

727
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:58,720
and see if there's anything

728
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:01,400
you want to add to it?

729
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,320
Let's take a look.

730
00:24:02,320 --> 00:24:02,840
Do you want

731
00:24:02,840 --> 00:24:04,000
to wipe your hands?

732
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:04,680
I'm okay.

733
00:24:05,160 --> 00:24:06,280
Are your hands clean?

734
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:06,800
They're clean.

735
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:08,720
There's a lot here.

736
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:09,960
They're all in these small containers.

737
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:15,080
Are we really stuffing these things in?

738
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:17,000
Yeah, squishing them
into the slime feels good.

739
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:17,880
Just add these in

740
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:18,800
and squish it around.

741
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:19,400
Take a look.

742
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:23,600
I think this would feel great.

743
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:24,920
This fine sand.

744
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:26,480
Yeah.

745
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,080
Or see if there are any

746
00:24:29,080 --> 00:24:30,480
fun shapes you like.

747
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,560
Aren't there red stones on your table?

748
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:35,640
I think the ones on the table are nice.

749
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,000
I think this one is good.

750
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,000
This would go well in mine.

751
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:42,040
This actually suits you.

752
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:42,640
Yeah.

753
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:43,800
I like this one.

754
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:45,760
This is popcorn.

755
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:47,240
That works.

756
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:48,400
What is this?

757
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:50,560
Have you tried the shrimp and fish cake

758
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:51,600
instant noodles?

759
00:24:51,600 --> 00:24:52,640
Is that fish cake?

760
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:54,200
I thought it was a crab stick.

761
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,760
That's just what the noodles are called.

762
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:56,920
Alright.

763
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:59,840
Did you ever make
instant noodles at school?

764
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,520
I did.

765
00:25:00,520 --> 00:25:01,960
There was a time when I was really into

766
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,800
one that came with three
seasoning packets.

767
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,240
We bought several cases

768
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:07,560
and split them among my close friends.

769
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:09,160
You guys can really eat.

770
00:25:11,300 --> 00:25:11,900
(Staring)

771
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:15,480
You're sprinkling it so ceremoniously.

772
00:25:15,540 --> 00:25:17,000
(Cracks up)

773
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,160
It's like you're cooking.

774
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:20,320
But it looks pretty good.

775
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:21,200
What is it?

776
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,120
I'm sprinkling in some glitter.

777
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:22,800
There's glitter too?

778
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:24,200
I didn't know that was glitter.
Want some?

779
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:24,680
Yeah.

780
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:26,720
Does yellow look good here? Hold on.

781
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:27,200
(Stops immediately)

782
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:27,720
It looks good.

783
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:28,600
Looks good? Okay.

784
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:30,040
Here.

785
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:31,000
Let's just sprinkle it around.

786
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,080
Just a little.

787
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:33,360
That's too much?

788
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,160
A bit more.

789
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,720
I feel like I'm sprinkling salt on food.

790
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:37,680
That's enough. Thanks.

791
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,600
Okay.

792
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:39,420
(Rolling)

793
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:40,940
(Rolling)

794
00:25:40,940 --> 00:25:42,320
I feel like I'm making pancakes.

795
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,360
Yeah.

796
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:44,840
Do you like to eat...

797
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:46,400
Pancakes?

798
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,520
Egg pancakes.

799
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:48,640
I actually like them.

800
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,240
I like them too.

801
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:51,120
My favorite

802
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:53,040
egg pancake place shut down.

803
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:54,400
I was so sad.

804
00:25:54,420 --> 00:25:55,280
(Looking)

805
00:25:55,280 --> 00:25:56,120
There used to be

806
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:57,280
an amazing egg pancake place

807
00:25:57,280 --> 00:25:58,760
over by Jianwai SOHO.

808
00:26:00,680 --> 00:26:02,080
You like egg pancakes too?
What a coincidence.

809
00:26:02,080 --> 00:26:02,880
I really do.

810
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,280
But later on, I didn't get
to have them as often

811
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:06,400
because not many places sell them.

812
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:06,760
Exactly.

813
00:26:06,760 --> 00:26:08,440
When I was younger, even in high school,

814
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:10,240
I ate them every single day.

815
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:12,560
I ate them in high school because
I took classes over there.

816
00:26:14,560 --> 00:26:16,040
I see.

817
00:26:18,040 --> 00:26:19,320
Okay.

818
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:20,240
Really good.

819
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,280
Well then...

820
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:22,280
A perfect finish.

821
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:24,240
A perfect ending.

822
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:26,400
Let's go.

823
00:26:30,740 --> 00:26:32,740
(Stay tuned for more sparks
next episode)
